                        <h4 class="title">ISO 45001 CERTIFICATION : HEALTH & SAFETY MANAGEMENT SYSTEMS</h4>
                        <p >ISO 45001 Certification Occupational health and safety management systems (OHSMS), is a latest worldwide standard which will provide a framework for organizations/company to improve employee Health ,safety, reduce workplace accidental risks and create better, secure working conditions, all over the world. ISO45001 Standard will follow the high level Annex SL-structure that has been applied to other ISO Certification management system standards currently updated, such as ISO 9001:2015 and ISO 14001 Certification.<br />ISO 45001 Certification has been developed with the industrial and modernization developments the health hazards and accidents due to negligence has been continuing to increase day by day. Due to this the death rate continues to be increasing day by day. ISO 45001 Certification enables the organization to demonstrate to their customers, workers, regulators and the community that they proactively as systematically manage the health and safety of their workers.<br />ISO 45001 has been published on 12th March 2018. ISO 45001 Certification is the worldâ€™s first OHS international Certification and provides emphasis on the active participation to minimize harm to workers through Leadership and Participation, understanding the context of the business taking action to manage risk by following all the requirements of ISO 45001 Certification international standard and getting certified.</p>
